! mcp_bootstrap_p89.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 89:
! the tail of the IOD-card field scan (DENSITY and DISPOSITION), and
! the head of "IS THIS IOD IN THE UNIT NAME TABLE".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.96, header "PAGE NUMBER 89",
! LOCATION 005053 printed in the column header.
!
! Fifty-six printed lines.  FORTY-SEVEN COMPILE; lines 2, 13, 26 and
! 30-35 carry only the dash in the STATEMENT column (30-35 are the
! boxed banner "IS THIS IOD IN THE UNIT NAME TABLE").
!
! CONTIGUOUS BY ADDRESS.  The page's first located line is 1 at
! 005053.40 and its last is 56 at 005114.00, two half words long, so
! printed p.90 must begin at 005115.00.  Every link in between closes:
! each row's location plus one half word per "XXXXXX.NN NN" group in
! its BINARY OUTPUT equals the next row's location, all forty-six
! links, with no gap and no overlap.  This is what says no line was
! dropped off the top or the bottom of the render.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE DOES.  Lines 1-23 are two copies of one loop.  Each
! loads a type-scan index (T SCIX3 for density, T SCIX4 for
! disposition), compares the IOD card's field against the scan table
! with KF under progressive indexing, steps the index by the backup
! constant on a mismatch, and on a match connects the matched code
! into the card's two-bit CODE field (T IDNCD, T IDSCD).  A scan that
! runs off the end bumps T MXGA -- the error count -- by 2 for density
! and by 1 for disposition.  Line 24 saves that flag in T ERFLG and
! lines 25-29 reject the card if the TYPE code is invalid.  Lines
! 36-56 then walk the UNIT NAME TABLE looking for this IOD's channel
! name, equipment type and (for tape) unit name.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- WHICH ARE TRANSCRIBED AND WHICH ARE DERIVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) ALREADY TRANSCRIBED ELSEWHERE, and confirmed a second time by
!     this page's own BINARY OUTPUT column.  Every field offset below
!     is printed in this page's address field and matches
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p84.strap's !SYM block exactly:
!
!       line  1  T IMOCD  000006.76        line 37  T IREF   000000.64
!       line  4  T IDN    000007.00        line 45  T ICH    000004.00
!       line 12  T IDNCD  000007.76        line 46  T IUN    000005.00
!       line 15  T IDS    000010.00        line 47  T ITYCD  000002.74
!       line 23  T IDSCD  000010.76        line 50  T CHNM   000000.00
!       line 27  T ITYCD  000002.74        line 52  T UNTYP  000000.74
!       line 36  T UNXW   004653.00        line 56  T UNME   000031.00
!
!     and from decks/mcp_bootstrap_p83.strap:
!
!       line 24  T ERFLG  004632.00  (printed 004632.27 30)
!       line 41  T LIMB   002155.00  (printed 002155.00 80)
!       line 54  T DKSAV  004652.00  (printed 004652.21 30)
!       the index names T MX1=$1, T MXC=$4, T MXG=$8, T MXI=$10,
!       T MXGA=$11 -- each confirmed here by the register offset the
!       address field prints (.21 for $8, .27 for $11, two per
!       register, exactly as printed p.80 line 28's V+ICR,T IXG).
!
! (b) NOT YET TRANSCRIBED, recovered from this page's own binary
!     column where the instruction's low octal field is a FIXED
!     constant calibrated on this page:
!
!       LX / V+ print ".20"  (lines 3, 14, 36 against T UNXW)
!         line  3  004757.20 10  -> T SCIX3 = 004757.00
!         line 10  004760.20 B0  -> T SCBK3 = 004760.00
!         line 14  004762.20 10  -> T SCIX4 = 004762.00
!         line 21  004763.20 B0  -> T SCBK4 = 004763.00
!         >>> ALL FOUR CONFIRMED INDEPENDENTLY. <<<  printed p.86 was
!         transcribed while this page was, and its !SYM block prints
!         T SCIX3 004757.00, T SCBK3 004760.00, T SCIX4 004762.00 and
!         T SCBK4 004763.00 off its own LOCATION column -- the same
!         four values this page's address field gives.
!       B prints ".10"  (lines 9, 20 against on-page T GET3/T GET4)
!         line 40  005377.10 00  -> T MREJB = 005377.00
!       BZXCZ prints ".30"  (lines 7, 18 against T MLOK3/T MLOK4)
!         line 49  005116.30 42  -> T M1E   = 005116.00
!         -- one notch weaker than the rest of this bucket: line 49
!         is BXCZ, not BZXCZ.  What carries the constant across the
!         pair is printed p.80, where BZXF and BXF both print ".23"
!         (its lines 6 and 27), so the Z prefix does not move the low
!         field.  The assembler reproduces 005116.30 42 from 5116.0.
!       BZB prints ".34"  (printed p.80 line 10, BZB -> T P1B)
!         line 55  005162.34 00  -> T M1D   = 005162.00
!
!     >>> THE LOW FIELD OF A BRANCH IS NOT THE TARGET'S OFFSET. <<<
!     Line 38's "BZRZ,T MEAT" prints 005100.74 and T MEAT is at
!     005100.40 -- the .74 carries the condition as well.  Each
!     constant above was therefore calibrated against a target this
!     page or an already-transcribed page states outright, never
!     assumed.
!
! (c) ONE DERIVED VALUE, AND IT IS MARKED.  T M1B is reached only by
!     BZAE (lines 51 and 53, both printing 005115.76), and this page
!     has no BZAE to a known target.  5115.40 is what reproduces the
!     printed bytes under the assembler; 5115.00 would print
!     005115.36.  THE ASSEMBLER, NOT THE PAGE, IS THE AUTHORITY FOR
!     THIS ONE VALUE -- when printed p.90 is read, T M1B's own
!     LOCATION line settles it.
!
! THREE LISTING MARKS: the asterisk after the location on lines 1, 20
! and 44, recorded as printed and not interpreted here.

! ---- index names, printed p.83 ------------------------------------
TMX1    SYN, $1
TMXC    SYN, $4
TMXG    SYN, $8
TMXGA   SYN, $11
TMXI    SYN, $10

! ---- words, printed p.83 ------------------------------------------
TERFLG  SYN, (8)4632.0
TDKSAV  SYN, (8)4652.0
TLIMB   SYN, (8)2155.0

! ---- the unit name table and its offsets, printed p.84 ------------
TUNXW   SYN, (8)4653.0
TCHNM   SYN(BU,48), 0.0
TUNTYP  SYN(BU,4), 0.60
TUNME   SYN(BU,48), 25.0

! ---- IOD card breakdown table offsets, printed p.84 ---------------
TIREF   SYN(BU,12), 0.52
TITYCD  SYN(BU,4), 2.60
TICH    SYN(BU,48), 4.0
TIUN    SYN(BU,48), 5.0
TIMOCD  SYN(BU,2), 6.62
TIDN    SYN(BU,12), 7.0
TIDNCD  SYN(BU,2), 7.62
TIDS    SYN(BU,30), 8.0
TIDSCD  SYN(BU,2), 8.62

! ---- off page, read out of THIS page's binary column --------------
TSCIX3  SYN, (8)4757.0
TSCBK3  SYN, (8)4760.0
TSCIX4  SYN, (8)4762.0
TSCBK4  SYN, (8)4763.0
TMREJB  SYN, (8)5377.0
TM1E    SYN, (8)5116.0
TM1D    SYN, (8)5162.0
TM1B    SYN, (8)5115.40           ! DERIVED -- see (c) above

        SLC, (8)5053.40

! ---- THE DENSITY FIELD SCAN --------------------------------------
        CM0101, TIMOCD(TMXI)         ! line 1
        LX, TMXG, TSCIX3             ! line 3  -LOAD FOR DENSITY SCAN
        C0011, TIDN(TMXI)            ! line 4
TMLOK3  KF(V+IC)(BU,12,6), 0.14(TMXG) ! line 5
        BAE, TMOK3                   ! line 6
        BZXCZ, TMLOK3                ! line 7
        V+I, TMXGA, 02.0             ! line 8  - A DENSITY FIELD ERROR
        B, TGET3                     ! line 9
TMOK3   V+, TMXG, TSCBK3             ! line 10
TGET3   C0011(BU,2), 0.0(TMXG)       ! line 11
        CM0101, TIDNCD(TMXI)         ! line 12

! ---- THE DISPOSITION FIELD SCAN ----------------------------------
        LX, TMXG, TSCIX4             ! line 14 -LOAD FOR DISP SCAN
        C0011, TIDS(TMXI)            ! line 15
TMLOK4  KF(V+IC)(BU,30,6), 0.33(TMXG) ! line 16
        BAE, TMOK4                   ! line 17
        BZXCZ, TMLOK4                ! line 18
        V+I, TMXGA, 01.0             ! line 19 - A DISPOSITION FIELD ERROR
        B, TGET4                     ! line 20
TMOK4   V+, TMXG, TSCBK4             ! line 21
TGET4   C0011(BU,3), 0.0(TMXG)       ! line 22
        CM0101, TIDSCD(TMXI)         ! line 23
TMNG    SV, TMXGA, TERFLG            ! line 24 -SAVE ERROR FLAG IF ANY
        BXVZ, TM1AA                  ! line 25 -IF THE CARD IS OK
        L, TITYCD(TMXI)              ! line 27 -CHECK FOR INVALID TYPE CODE
        BZRZ, TM1AA                  ! line 28 -TYPE CODE OK
        BD, $                        ! line 29 -MCP ERROR, INVALID TYPE CODE

! ---- IS THIS IOD IN THE UNIT NAME TABLE --------------------------
TM1AA   LX, TMXG, TUNXW              ! line 36 -LOAD TO BEGINNING OF
                                      !          UNIT NAME TABLE
        L, TIREF(TMXI), 46           ! line 37 -GET THE REFERENCE NUMBER
        BZRZ, TMEAT                  ! line 38 -NO
TMDOG   LVI, TMX1, 8.0               ! line 39 -ILLEGAL REF NO. ON AN
                                      !          IOD CARD
        B, TMREJB                    ! line 40
TMEAT   +(BU,18), TLIMB, 46          ! line 41 -COMPUTE THE SIOL ADDRESS
        LV, TMXC, $R                 ! line 42 -ADDRESS OF SIOL TO IX
        LF(BU), 0.0(TMXC)            ! line 43 -IS SIOL SLOT ALREADY USED
        BZRZ, TMDOG                  ! line 44 -YES - REPORT ILLEGAL IOD
                                      !          CARD TO JC
        L, TICH(TMXI), 16            ! line 45 -GET CHAN FIELD OF IOD CARD
        LF, TIUN(TMXI), 80           ! line 46 -GET THE UNIT NAME -
                                      !          TAPE ONLY
        LF, TITYCD(TMXI)             ! line 47 -GET THE TYPE FIELD CODED
        V+I, TMXG, 0.0               ! line 48 -TO RE-ACTIVATE INDEX
                                      !          IND. FOR T MXG
        BXCZ, TM1E                   ! line 49 -IF ZERO ENTRY
TM1A    KF, TCHNM(TMXG), 16          ! line 50 -COMPARE AGAINST TABLE
        BZAE, TM1B                   ! line 51 -IF UNLIKE ENTRY
        KF, TUNTYP(TMXG)             ! line 52 -COMPARE EQUIP FEILD
        BZAE, TM1B                   ! line 53 -IF NOT ALIKE
        SV, TMXG, TDKSAV             ! line 54
        BZB, TITYCD(TMXI), TM1D      ! line 55 -IF NOT TAPE
        KF, TUNME(TMXG), 80          ! line 56 -TAPE COMPARE UNIT NAME

